<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">title: "How Much Should a Roof Replacement Cost? Real Numbers &amp; What to Expect in 2024" description: "Wondering if your roofing quote is fair? Get real data on roof replacement costs by size, material, and region—plus red flags that signal overcharging." date: 2024-01-15 author: Ungouge Team keywords: ["how much should a roof replacement cost", "roof replacement cost", "roofing prices", "asphalt shingle cost", "metal roof cost", "roofing quote red flags"]</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h1 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.1px 0.0px; font: 24.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #138756; -webkit-text-stroke: #138756"><span class="s1"><b>How Much Should a Roof Replacement Cost? Real Numbers &amp; What to Expect in 2024</b></span></h1>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">You've just received a quote for a roof replacement, and the number makes your stomach drop. Is $15,000 reasonable—or are you being taken for a ride?</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">The frustrating truth is that roofing prices vary wildly, and most homeowners have no idea what they should actually be paying. Contractors know this. And some exploit it.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">This guide cuts through the noise with real data: Bureau of Labor Statistics wage information, actual material costs, and regional variations that affect your bottom line. No vague ranges or affiliate links to "get three quotes" services. Just the facts you need to evaluate whether your quote is fair.</span></p>
<h2 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.9px 0.0px; font: 18.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0f6745; -webkit-text-stroke: #0f6745"><span class="s1"><b>The Real Cost of Roof Replacement by Size</b></span></h2>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Let's start with the numbers that matter most. Here's what you should expect to pay for a complete roof replacement using asphalt shingles (the most common material) in 2024:</span></p>
<table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="t1">
