<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h2 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.9px 0.0px; font: 18.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0f6745; -webkit-text-stroke: #0f6745"><span class="s1"><b>Final Thoughts: Pay Fairly, Not Blindly</b></span></h2>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">A roof replacement is one of the most significant home investments you'll make. You deserve to know whether you're paying a fair market price or getting gouged.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">The data in this guide gives you a baseline. Regional variation, roof complexity, and material choices all affect final cost—but they shouldn't double your price without explanation.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Get multiple quotes. Ask questions. Verify insurance. And if something feels off, trust your gut.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Most contractors are honest. But the ones who aren't are counting on your confusion. Don't give them the opportunity.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Know your numbers. Protect your investment.</b></span></p>
